      "username": "Koga",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/koga/{size}/2058_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-08-15T00:17:12.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"McBehrer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/48/1850_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> McBehrer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>They are also not removed from play when The Operative or the player next to them are incapacitated. They can only be removed by their own text.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>During playtesting, it was confirmed that the poisons stay when Operative is incapped but not when the player that's poisoned is incapped.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"lutherbellhendricksv\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lutherbellhendricksv/48/2350_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> lutherbellhendricksv:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>When someone is incapacitated, you basically wipe their board. Powers, tokens, everything. The poisons too.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>",
